WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.870
Just around the time the sun began
to fall and dyed the earth red,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:23.790
the nomad continued on his journey
and found the hummingbird dying.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.590
He could have just walked by,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.390
but the nomad stopped
and spoke to the hummingbird.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:37.220
Joe! Joe! Joe! Joe!

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.980
"Say, Hummingbird.
I may have the eyes to see you,

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.860
ears to hear your song,
a mouth to speak to you,

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:53.070
the hands to shoo you away,
and the legs to take me on this journey,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.330
but I've lost everything else."

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.040
"I truly have nothing else."

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:14.390
"And then... the dying hummingbird
replied... in a faint voice."

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.390
And then, the dying hummingbird
replied in a faint voice,

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.890
"That is a lie.
You have a past to regret,

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.890
"That is a lie... You have a past..."

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.560
a present you can choose,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.360
and an undetermined future.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:31.490
To a soul that is dying like me, you still
have everything left in this world."

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.740
"Yes, you are right. You win again.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.000
Now, sing for me."

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:45.830
The nomad sat down
next to the bird, awaiting its song,

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.420
but he doesn't hear a thing.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:53.590
The hummingbird had already passed on.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.600
I'm the one who did this to you!

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.060
I ended up signing the contract
in exchange for Miguel's surgery.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:07.730
And because of that, you're now at the top
of the Megalo-boxing world,

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.400
and a hero.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:14.740
You've achieved something
your former self never could've reached.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.170
You're not just some onlooker

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.710
looking up at a legend anymore.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.970
You're a true hero.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.220
Hero, my ass.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.980
"Team Nowhere"

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.740
Listen up.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:21.320
What I'm about to teach you
isn't how to defeat Mac.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.200
It's how you're going to survive
and come back here.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.700
Don't even think about
going punch for punch with him.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.830
Yeah.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.250
Don't go throwing any punches.
Concentrate on your defense.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.000
What? I don't get to attack at all?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.510
You'll learn to use defense
to break down your opponent.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.260
Swing without swinging.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:40.130
The basics of boxing.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.300
All right, fine.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.180
If you manage to get a hit in,
I'll treat you to ramen at First Star.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.230
You never stop talking, do you?

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.350
Begin.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.860
Don't stand right in front of him.
Spread yourself out in that ring.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.120
Talk about some impressive Gear.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.790
The leather on the outside
absorbs the impact from a punch,

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.170
lessening the damage.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:16.340
They really put a lot of thought into it.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.050
But because it concentrates
so much on defense,

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.550
it really limits the movement on the arms.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:28.720
Cowhide is sturdy,
but too stiff to use flexibly.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.440
Chief had the build
and the strength to use it,

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.440
but it puts Joe at a disadvantage.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:35.900
I see.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.360
What should we do?

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.200
First, we'll rebuild this Gear,

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.280
and expand how much
range of motion his arms have. And...

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.700
I thought we could use this.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.370
Deerskin, eh?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.710
This is sturdy yet soft, and it'll be able
to keep up with Joe's moves.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.130
I guess we know what we're doing then.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:13.270
Guess his time in the ring
didn't go to complete waste.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.310
Yeah.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:20.730
And no one watched Joe closer than Sachio.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.960
I think the moment you stop because
you realize you've made a mistake

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.460
is also taking a step towards the future.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.970
They had a jumper, I guess.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.310
"Another youth who had lost all hope."

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.060
How stupid can you be?

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.060
Expecting something from the future

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.480
but giving up your opportunity
to create it yourself.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.820
Is it so wrong to expect something?

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.780
Believing you can reach
the future you believed in

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.450
by being positive and working hard.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:17.120
You weren't thinking of
jumping, too, were you?

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:23.960
I was gathering my thoughts
so I could refute Professor Shirato.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:27.130
Nice. That's a great idea.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:30.600
Give that ignorant ass
a piece of our mind.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.510
He needs to find out
his moldy sense of ethics

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.390
won't be enough to stop
the evolution of technology.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.230
Mr. Sakuma.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:43.190
Do you think Mac will come back?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.620
You need either pleasure
or fear to drive people.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.080
Mac had lost everything once.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.910
He knows that fear very well.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.290
Think he's brave enough
to lose it all again?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.130
Shirato Group
Head of the Corporate Planning Office

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.440
Daddy will be back.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:25.440
The hummingbird will
show him the way back.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:28.990
You're right.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.450
We need to get you to bed.

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.930
Do you want some water?

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:02.980
They said they'll be done with
the inspection on the Gear soon.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.270
Are you done?

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.120
Thanks, Maya.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.410
Where's this coming from?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:24.790
I'm able to move again
because of Mr. Sakuma.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.760
I was even able to get
back into Megalo-boxing.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.590
But the real me... Well, look at me.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:38.020
I can't even drink water on my own.
I'm completely powerless.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:44.310
The only reason I'm alive
is because of you, Maya.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.500
What's the matter?
Why are you parked here?

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:12.340
That doesn't concern you.
Just leave me alone.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.140
Does this car belong to you?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.440
I'll need to see your ID.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.980
Step out of the vehicle.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.820
Come on, hurry up!

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.530
Do as I say!

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.110
Tanaka!

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.280
Don't talk to them like that!

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.280
But, sir...

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.700
He wasn't cooperating.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:45.170
No matter who we're dealing with,
they live in this town, just like us.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:48.960
We need to treat everyone
with respect, don't we?

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.260
Is that you, Mac?

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:57.970
Mac, it's me! Hakeem!

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.470
Partner...

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.240
Thanks, man.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.950
Um...

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:28.670
I'm sorry about earlier.
I didn't realize who you were.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:33.380
It's all right. I was in a bad mood.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:38.470
He's a Megalo-boxer, too.
He's the young hopeful on our squad.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:39.850
I see.

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:43.100
I saw your title match the other day.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.850
It sure is something.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.060
When we used to practice
together at the gym,

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.980
I guess I was impressed
that you were a former pro,

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.940
but I never thought you'd
make it all the way to the top!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.650
I'll find a group of brats out on
the streets while on patrol.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.740
They won't listen to a damn word I say,

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:04.200
but I show them this picture
and they get a gleam in their eyes.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:09.330
Everyone knows about you, Mac.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:15.510
You are the police officer who put
his life on the line to save those kids.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:20.220
That's right. Mac Rosario
is our local hero.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:25.060
If I actually died back there,
I might've actually ended up a hero.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:29.020
Did something happen?

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.810
Nah.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.280
There was nothing to begin with.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:46.620
I can't help but wonder
if I could've done the same thing

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.620
if I was in your position back there.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.800
I'm pretty sure my knees would've buckled.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:01.300
Do I have the same kind of courage you do?

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:04.850
I might've lost both you and Miguel.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.220
I just...

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.790
Damn it!

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.410
Here you go.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.380
Application Requirements

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:44.470
Here you go.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.550
Thanks.

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:51.060
You good?

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:54.940
Daddy!

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.270
I'm home.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.860
There's no other way to treat him
other than transplant surgery.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.410
Damn it!

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.700
I've arrived at the scene!

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:07.870
My children are inside!

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:08.870
Don't!

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.920
Come on!

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:20.050
Mommy!

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:22.380
Hey, Mac! Are you all right?

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.300
Mac!

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.640
Daddy!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.420
That has nothing to do with courage.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:07.090
I was scared that I could lose everything
precious to me at any moment.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.100
Hey, Mac. Where're you going?

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.270
Home.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.900
That song brought back memories

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:34.710
The nomad buried the hummingbird
on the side of the road

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:38.750
and sung the hummingbird's song
as if to mourn its loss.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:43.010
He found that singing
that song eased his soul

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:46.050
and he continued to walk as he sang.

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:49.890
Eventually, he had finally
reached the ocean.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:56.850
The nomad asked the quiet ocean
as it reflected the starry sky,

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:01.610
"I am a nomad who walked
a long way to get here.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:05.900
Could you grant me my wish?"

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:10.160
The ocean splashed
a small wave and replied,

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.660
"Those who come here with wishes
ask for the same things.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.460
Either money, fame, or death.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:19.080
Which do you desire?"

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:23.420
Then the nomad replied
with a beaming face,

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:27.010
"I once had everything,

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:30.390
so I desire none of those things."

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:36.980
"I just want to be shown
the way back home."

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:45.030
Was the nomad able to go back home?

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:49.740
No matter how far he went,
his heart is still connected.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:52.410
That's why I'm sure he'll make it home.

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:09.220
Mac...

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:15.850
I thought maybe you
wouldn't come home again.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.230
I'm sorry I made you worry.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:19.520
I'm so sorry.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.020
It's all my fault.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.350
That's not true.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.020
Back then, if I were in your shoes,

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.440
I would've done the same.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:33.950
You actually saved Miguel's life
when I couldn't do anything.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:39.580
Bad things only happen
so something good can happen.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:43.170
My grandma used to say that
all the time when I was a kid.

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.840
I haven't lost anything.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.550
Daddy!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.760
Welcome home, Daddy!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.100
I'm back, Miguel.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:57.560
See? I told you.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.480
Come, now.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:03.770
Sorry I made you worry.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:07.650
Daddy, your beard is all scruffy!
It looks funny!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:14.530
There's something we have to do
in order for us to move ahead.

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:49.020
<i>¡Hola! </i>Welcome back, Mac!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.150
I'm not actually back.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:55.110
I came here to tell you

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:59.240
that I'm going to fight Joe my own way.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.200
Your own way?

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.830
I'll play my role
as your mascot until the end.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:08.040
You should be satisfied with that.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:12.840
Oh, I see. I figured this day would come.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:15.090
Do what you want.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:18.930
I basically got everything
I could get out of you.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:23.680
Oh, but make sure you beat Joe.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.190
Even if this is the end,

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:29.440
don't do anything to drag
ROSCO's name down with you.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:31.530
<i>Adios, amigo.</i>

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:39.120
Come on! Push! No time to rest, Mac!

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.660
I don't see those feet moving!

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:56.590
We'd had a conversation here before.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:20:01.930
That's when you told me there was
a young boxer with a lot of potential.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.220
I guess you were talking about Liu.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.980
Yeah.

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:07.560
How's he doing?

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:12.190
He'll be starting PT soon.
He hasn't given up a single thing.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.490
I see.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:25.120
I never thought I'd be having a
conversation with you here again.

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:29.960
They call me the Raging Bull!
Say your prayers, Matador!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:33.670
I'll break off your horns
and turn you into beef curry!

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.420
I'd like to see you try!

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:36.420
This is the light that you brought us.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:41.140
Hey, come back here!

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:41.140
I'll never despair in the future again.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:44.680
So you better not die, Joe.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:48.520
Yeah.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:57.310
"Team Nowhere"

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:54.230
Joe! Yuri! Chowtime!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.780
Come on, let's hurry up and eat.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:56.940
Yeah.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.340
Miguel.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:26.430
Make sure you watch your dad
out there in that ring.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.520
Okay.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:31.560
Don't worry.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.480
We've got your back.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.740
I guess it's still here.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.740
I hope you're watching us, Pops.

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:49.620
"Team"

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.950
Let's go, Sachio.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:50.620
Yeah.

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:53.830
"Team Nowhere"

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:02.720
Oh?

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.020
You actually showed up.

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:37.580
"Team Nowhere"
